# Test: a live edit of service { image-server } reaches the image server.
# Initial config: image-server enabled with image-directory /srv/ze-img-a.
# After SIGHUP:   image-directory is /srv/ze-img-b, nothing else changes.
# Expected: imageserver installs the reloaded config at apply and logs it with
#           the new image directory.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 26, AC-1: imageserver's
#            verify/apply pair replaces its HTTP servers for the reloaded
#            config (imageServer.install).
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while the server kept serving the boot image-directory.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the "/srv/ze-img-b" line is written only by install, which
# only the apply handler calls on a reload: without the handler the second
# expectation fails. That an edit elsewhere under service replaces no server
# is proven in Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop
# (imageserver/config_tx_test.go). The listener names an interface that does
# not exist, so its address does not resolve and that is logged; the reload
# asserts the install, not the socket.

option=env:var=ze.log.imageserver:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	image-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface ze-no-such-iface0
		image-directory /srv/ze-img-a
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	image-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface ze-no-such-iface0
		image-directory /srv/ze-img-b
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete:then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=imageserver: config applied.*image-directory=/srv/ze-img-a
expect=stderr:pattern=imageserver: config applied.*image-directory=/srv/ze-img-b
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
